/-!
# VII-06 (F3a, part A): charged-tail nondegeneracy

On the actual `PaperData` + `FactorizedN` + `PaperBVP` branch with the independent VII-05
`SmoothBranch` extension `(F, b, Aext)` and `Q ≠ 0`, the actual `f, m, N` and the actual Maxwell
discriminant `alphaSq` are positive on a smaller radial tail `R > s + δ⁻¹`.

Route: the compact core `alphaCore Q h F b Aext x = Q² F² - x (1 - h x) b F (Aext')²` has no
division at `x = 0`, is continuous there (smoothness of the extensions) and equals `Q²` at `0`. For
`0 < x < ε` the real chart identity `(1 - h x) b(x) alphaSq(s + 1/x) = 4 x³ alphaCore(x)` holds,
obtained from `f = F`, `m = b/x`, `N = (1 - h x)/x²` and `a'(s + 1/x) = -x² Aext'(x)` (open-set
`Set.EqOn.deriv` + the VII-04 real chain rule `deltaFun_pull_a`). No `G = 0`, Kerr–Schild premise,
Taylor expansion or literal `pullM` at `x = 0` is used. Positivity is only eventual: no claim is made
for the whole exterior, and `Q = 0` branches are not covered.
-/

